.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-migrate 1  "rev-stealth-config-migrate " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-migrate \- P6.3: Migrate `policy.toml` (and authorized.toml) from its current `schema_version` to the latest known version. v1 → v1 is a no\-op (returns exit 0 + an audit\-trail line). The harness is in place for future v2+ migrations to plug into
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config migrate\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Migrate policy.toml + authorized.toml from their current schema_version to the latest known version. v1 → v1 is a no\-op (exit 0 + audit\-trail line). \-\-dry\-run prints the migration plan without writing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config migrate
  $ rev\-stealth config migrate \-\-dry\-run

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Migration completed (or no\-op).
  1  UserError        Schema not migratable / unsupported version.
  3  PermanentError   ConfigWriter IO failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_POLICY      Override the policy.toml path.
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTHORIZED  Override the authorized.toml path.
